{# The contextual help button (ARCHITECTURE.md §8.64) — ALWAYS visible,
   included once, at the right of the breadcrumb bar
   (partials/breadcrumb_bar.html.twig), which since the mega-menu rework
   shows at every width, mobile, desktop browser and installed PWA alike.
   (The original plan doubled it into the desktop nav's right-hand group,
   back when the breadcrumb bar was hidden in a desktop browser tab —
   that would now put two identical buttons on screen at once.)

   Two shapes, one look:
   - A topic covers the current page → a <button> opening the offcanvas
     panel (partials/help_panel.html.twig, rendered by base.html.twig
     exactly when route_help is non-empty).
   - No topic → a plain link to /aide, so the help index is reachable
     from every page. Never hidden: a hidden button was the mockup's
     behaviour, and it left /aide unreachable from anywhere.

   `route_help` is the Twig global Core\Http\FrontController sets after
   the RBAC guard — already role-filtered, already rendered. #}
{% if route_help|default([]) is not empty %}
    <button type="button"
            class="btn btn-link p-1 border-0 text-body-secondary d-inline-flex align-items-center"
            data-bs-toggle="offcanvas"
            data-bs-target="#help-panel"
            aria-controls="help-panel"
            title="Aide sur cette page">
        <i class="bi bi-question-circle" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span class="visually-hidden">Aide sur cette page</span>
    </button>
{% else %}
    <a href="/aide"
       class="btn btn-link p-1 border-0 text-body-secondary d-inline-flex align-items-center"
       title="Aide">
        <i class="bi bi-question-circle" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span class="visually-hidden">Aide</span>
    </a>
{% endif %}
